<title>GERMANY: Hugo Boss details 1996 results. [CORRECTED 14:13 GMT]</title>
<headline>Hugo Boss details 1996 results. [CORRECTED 14:13 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>METZINGEN, Germany 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar year 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   76.100  up 58.000</p>
<p>(Corrects 1996 group net profit from &quot;75.200&quot;)</p>
<p>    Return on sales after tax		7.6     vs 6.4 pct</p>
<p>    Return on equity			   29.0    vs 26.3 pct</p>
<p>    Group sales				  995.300 up 10.5 pct</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share DVFA	  107     vs 97 dmk</p>
<p>    Cash flow per share			152     vs 112 dmk</p>
<p>    Dividend on common shares		45	vs 41 dmk</p>
<p>    Dividend on preference shares	  46.50   vs 42.50 dmk</p>
<p>    Special dividend			   57	vs 0 dmk</p>
<p>    Group cash flow (adjusted)	     97.0    vs 71.5</p>
<p>    Free cash flow before dividend	 44.1    vs 90.9</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total			486.3   vs 422.3</p>
<p>    Shareholders equity			287.0   vs 237.9</p>
<p>    Equity to assets ratio		   59.0    vs 56.3 pct</p>
<p>    Workforce				    2,147   vs 2,104</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German retailing group is Hugo Boss AG. The group also said it planned to expand its portfolio by launching a collection for women between the ages of 20 and 40 in January 1998. It also plans to launch a perfume for women, Hugo woman, in August 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
